<p class="work-desc en">
  Developed HDCoin, a proof-of-useful-work blockchain framework that
  transforms conventional mining into useful training and verification
  of trustworthy biomedical Hyperdimensional Computing (HDC) models.
  The project explored distributed HDC training, model verification,
  adaptive mining difficulty, and fairness across biomedical learning tasks.
</p>

<p class="work-desc zh" style="display:none">
  开发 HDCoin，一种“有用工作量证明”（Proof-of-Useful-Work）区块链框架，
  将传统挖矿过程转化为可信生物医学超维计算（HDC）模型的有效训练与验证。
  项目研究了分布式 HDC 训练、模型验证、自适应挖矿难度以及生物医学学习任务中的公平性机制。
</p>

<ul class="work-bullets">
  <li class="en">
    Developed HDCoin, a proof-of-useful-work blockchain framework that
    transforms conventional mining into useful training of trustworthy
    biomedical Hyperdimensional Computing (HDC) models.
  </li>
  <li class="zh" style="display:none">
    开发 HDCoin，一种基于“有用工作量证明”的区块链框架，
    将传统挖矿转化为可信生物医学超维计算（HDC）模型的有效训练过程。
  </li>

  <li class="en">
    Designed HDC-based mining and verification pipelines where distributed
    miners train, validate, reproduce, and verify biomedical learning models
    using nonce-generated item memories and HDC hyperparameter configurations.
  </li>
  <li class="zh" style="display:none">
    设计基于 HDC 的挖矿与验证流程，使分布式矿工能够利用由 nonce 生成的
    Item Memory 和 HDC 超参数配置，对生物医学学习模型进行训练、验证、复现与校验。
  </li>

  <li class="en">
    Conducted design-space exploration across HDC dimensionality,
    retraining iterations, and retraining rates on four biomedical datasets:
    UCIHAR, BreastMNIST, PneumoniaMNIST, and NoduleMNIST3D.
  </li>
  <li class="zh" style="display:none">
    在 UCIHAR、BreastMNIST、PneumoniaMNIST 和 NoduleMNIST3D
    四个生物医学数据集上，对 HDC 维度、重训练迭代次数以及重训练率进行了设计空间探索。
  </li>

  <li class="en">
    Evaluated adaptive mining difficulty and fairness mechanisms, analyzing
    how HDC configurations affect computational effort, model performance,
    and miners' winning probability.
  </li>
  <li class="zh" style="display:none">
    评估自适应挖矿难度与公平性机制，分析不同 HDC 配置如何影响计算工作量、
    模型性能以及矿工获得区块奖励的概率。
  </li>
</ul>


